==English==
{{was wotd|2010|January|6}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|exigēns}}, present active participle of {{m|la|exigō||demand, require}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɛk.sɪ.dʒənt/|/ˈɛɡ.zɪ.dʒənt/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[urgent|Urgent]]; needing [[immediate]] [[action]].
#* '''2003''', [[s:Working Group Report on Detainee Interrogations|Working Group Report on Detainee Interrogations]], U.S. Department of Defence
#*: Article 2 also provides that acts of torture cannot be justified on the grounds of '''exigent''' circumstances, such as state of war or public emergency, or on orders from a superior officer or public authority.
# [[demanding|Demanding]]; needing great [[effort]].

